{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"HANDOFF STATE 2026-11-11 17:06 PST: OPEN, unsigned. Its prerequisite nickel-ferric-llama closed at 16:53 PST (merged fdf0a94aba8). First plan review (worktree CLI at fdf0a94aba8, Bedrock, 16:54-17:05 PST) returned BLOCK: 9 blocking and 20 advisory findings. They come down to 4 defects:\n(1) The plan says the adapted verdict flows through the \"unchanged post-dispatch path ... Pass-3 floors, advisory cap, sidecar emit and signing\". It doesn't: `_run_plan_review` runs `_apply_review_floors` only when engine == \"pipeline\", and the advisory cap lives in `orchestrator.partition_findings` (inside the pipeline's decide step), not after dispatch. State whether the adapter calls partition_findings/finalize_verdict with the cap, and whether the tail runs on agentic verdicts.\n(2) Tests outside Scope pin the interim behavior: tests/unit/test_plan_review_engine_switch.py `_assert_agentic_indeterminate` and tests/unit/test_plan_review_agentic.py assert INDETERMINATE plus `agentic-adapter-pending`. Add both to Scope. Also add src/rebar/llm/plan_review/agentic.py (`plan_review_agentic_verdict` is the op to replace) and the ADAPTER_PENDING_ID/coverage.agentic_findings references.\n(3) Failure handling: a failed agent step never reaches the adapter. It takes gate_dispatch's `_degraded_plan_review_verdict` (src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py), which records no `engine`. The epic wants engine plus failure class on coverage, so scope that path. There is no single \"resolution_class the pipeline uses\"; it is the closed failure-class enum from failure.outcome_of.\n(4) The \"unknown severity → advisory\" branch is unreachable, because the output contract already limits severity to the 4 values. Drop it or call it defensive. Cite partition_findings correctly (def ~:229) rather than finalize_verdict at :296-299.\nThe 7 carry-over advisories from change 3354 are in the previous comment. Next: revise the description (under 8,000 chars), then re-run review-plan. Not claimed."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1794445589970162355,"uuid":"8651e518-d5bb-41a2-869e-8e586fab670a"}